WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.859
What I love most about being up here is

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:10.980
simply being immersed in nature every

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.080
day, and being able to share that with

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.109
the students. The Biological Station is

00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:18.869
unique in that it gives students an

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:22.050
opportunity not to just merely learn things.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.960
Up here, I can showcase and demonstrate

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.990
the natural world biological phenomena,

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.240
and give students a real experience in

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.270
field biology. The primary course that I

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.070
teach every summer is General Ecology,

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.920
which is an introductory lecture-based

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.930
course with his little lecture as

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.760
possible. We'll have a three-hour lecture

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.219
and then we'll go out into the field and

00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:47.039
do a variety of lab activities--anything

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:49.590
from setting nets-trap nets out on the

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.840
lake to Blue Gill studies. We've gone

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.180
rafting down rivers. You read about a lot

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.370
of things in a biology textbook, but to

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.079
actually be out in the field and doing

00:00:58.079 --> 00:00:59.820
these things-the research element is so

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.699
much more real. One of the big advantages

00:01:02.699 --> 00:01:05.010
to Hillsdale College, throughout its

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:08.670
curriculum, is that we have a lot of the

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.299
opportunities, toys and things that big

00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:14.880
schools have, and unlike a lot of big

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.710
schools, our students actually get to use

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.830
them. For research, students get their own

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.890
project. I'm looking at the population

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.750
density of the redback salamanders. I

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.070
chose to do research here because I

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.689
enjoy being outside and working with

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:29.820
live animals instead of in a lab. We're

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.110
basically catching a whole bunch of them

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.860
and microchipping them and collecting data.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.080
because nobody's really studied these salamanders before.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.080
It's kind of a new project for Hillsdale College.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.720
I've had students invent new

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.900
field equipment, new field techniques. It's a very

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.180
real opportunity for students to go out

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:53.360
and see what ecologists do, not merely learn about it in a classroom.

